<title>USA: Hilton, Prudential close two deals.</title>
<headline>Hilton, Prudential close two deals.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp said Wednesday it has closed two transactions in which it acquired the majority of Prudential Insurance Co of America's interests in six hotels.</p>
<p>The first deal, with Prudential's General Account, involved the Chicago Hilton &amp; Towers and San Francisco Hilton &amp; Towers. The second, with Prudential's PRISA account, involved the New York Hilton &amp; Towers, Washington Hilton &amp; Towers, Capitol Hilton and Rye Town Hilton near New York City.</p>
<p>Hilton placed the total purchase price of the two transactions at $433 million.</p>
</text>
